Summary of US-106:
- **`generation.ts`**: New `getActiveRunSummary()` + `ActiveRunSummary` type + `currentStage` field on `GenerationRun`. Writes `<courseDir>/.generating.json` markers with `{childPid, slug, stage, startedAt}` at run start, on each child spawn, and on each `stage:started`; removes them in `finalize`. Cold-start reconciliation scans markers and probes PID liveness via `process.kill(pid, 0)`. Stale markers are unlinked inline.
- **`/api/courses/active-run`**: thin route returning `{active:false} | {active:true, slug, name, stage}`. Name resolved from `course.json#title` (preferred) or `course-spec.json#draftStructure.courseTitle` (fallback) or slug.
- **`/create` page**: sticky `ResumeBanner` ('Trwa generacja kursu <name> — <stage>' + 'Wróć do generacji') driven by mount-time fetch of active-run. New `?resume=<slug>` query support for the resume click. Banner hides when already on Stage 6 for the running slug. Removed `sendBeacon`-on-unmount cancel so tab close no longer kills the run.
- **Tests**: 12 new (5 in generation.test.ts, 7 in api.test.ts). All 572 vitest pass; typecheck clean.
- **Browser**: playwright drove the wizard end-to-end with `GENERATION_MOCK_INIT_DELAY_MS=15000` (new env knob), confirmed banner appears on return to /create with correct name/stage, click lands in Stage 6 with init_course log section visible, and dismiss (X) flow works in a fresh browser context.
